## Development

**Terms used:** [*datalab tool*](https://docs.datalab-org.io/tools-glossary/#datalab-tool), [*plugins.toml*](https://docs.datalab-org.io/tools-glossary/#plugins-toml).

Install it in a datalab checkout by adding it to the root `plugins.toml`:

```toml
dependencies = ["{{ distribution_name }}"]

[tool.uv.sources]
{{ distribution_name }} = { path = "../{{ distribution_name }}", editable = true }
```

{% if tool_ui_kind == "in-app" %}
Build the frontend before installing the Python package:

```shell
cd frontend
yarn install
yarn build
cd ..
```

The build creates
`src/{{ package_name }}/static/frontend/tool.js`. Commit the dependency
lockfile and this compiled artifact so a deployment administrator can review
and install the exact code that will run in users' browsers. During frontend
development, `yarn build:watch` rebuilds that file when its sources change;
refresh the *datalab tool* page to load it.
The source distribution includes the reviewable `frontend` sources and
lockfile, while the installed wheel contains only the compiled browser asset.
{% if add_item_table_action %}

This provider declares the *table-selection tool action*
**{{ item_table_action_label }}** for
